sched: the critical section monitor needs IRQCOUNT only for its csection and busy-wait parts

Purpose: SCHED_CRITMONITOR selects IRQCOUNT unconditionally.  On a single
CPU, IRQCOUNT turns enter_critical_section() and leave_critical_section()
from up_irq_save()/up_irq_restore() into function calls that also check for
interrupt context and count tcb->irqcount (sched/irq/irq_csection.c), on
every critical section in the OS.  Without SMP, the only readers of that
count are the critical section and busy-wait monitors
(SCHED_CRITMONITOR_MAXTIME_CSECTION or _BUSYWAIT >= 0: nxsched_switch_critmon()
and the enter/leave_critical_section() versions in irq_csection.c, which
include/nuttx/irq.h only declares under IRQCOUNT).  The per-task run time
and the CPU load (SCHED_CRITMONITOR_MAXTIME_THREAD >= 0,
SCHED_CPULOAD_CRITMONITOR) do not use it.

- sched/Kconfig: select IRQCOUNT only when one of those two monitors is on.
  SMP and SCHED_INSTRUMENTATION_CSECTION still select it themselves.

The board uses the monitor only for the CPU column of ps
(boards/arduino-nano-rp2040-connect/configs/imu/defconfig); with both
monitors off (-1, their defaults) the critical sections stay as they are
without SCHED_CRITMONITOR.
Zephyr: the Zephyr build's thread usage (CONFIG_SCHED_THREAD_USAGE) does
not touch irq_lock()/irq_unlock().

diff --git a/sched/Kconfig b/sched/Kconfig
index bac8e961..cc005153 100644
--- a/sched/Kconfig
+++ b/sched/Kconfig
@@ -922,7 +922,7 @@ config SCHED_IRQMONITOR
 config SCHED_CRITMONITOR
 	bool "Enable Critical Section monitoring"
 	default n
-	select IRQCOUNT
+	select IRQCOUNT if SCHED_CRITMONITOR_MAXTIME_CSECTION >= 0 || SCHED_CRITMONITOR_MAXTIME_BUSYWAIT >= 0
 	---help---
 		Enables logic that monitors the duration of time that a thread keeps
 		interrupts or pre-emption disabled.  These global locks can have
